## Data sources

Each source of data the application downloads or ships, who it is from, and on
what terms. Data marked "downloaded when you ask" is fetched from its owner by
your copy of the application and is never redistributed by this project.

<!-- credit: reference/adif -->
- **ADIF Development Group**: ADIF definitions, the fields, modes, bands and
  entities logs are checked against. Downloaded when you ask. Published for use
  by logging programs.
<!-- credit: reference/pota -->
- **Parks on the Air**: POTA parks, programs and locations. Downloaded when you
  ask. Public data, fetched from POTA and never redistributed.
<!-- credit: reference/sota -->
- **Summits on the Air**: SOTA summits, each summit's reference, name, height
  and position. Downloaded when you ask. Public data, fetched from SOTA and
  never redistributed.
<!-- credit: noaa -->
- **NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center**: solar flux, the K and A indices and
  the space weather scales, for Conditions. A work of the US Government, public
  domain.
<!-- credit: county/boundaries -->
- **US Census Bureau**: US county boundaries, to find the county a location is
  in. Ships with the application. A work of the US Government, public domain.
<!-- credit: county/names -->
- **ARRL's TQSL**: US county names as LoTW accepts them, from TQSL's
  configuration. Names only; TQSL's file is not included.
<!-- credit: county/sections -->
- **ARRL Section Boundaries**: ARRL sections and the counties each holds.
  Section assignments only; ARRL's page is not included.
<!-- credit: map/land -->
- **Natural Earth**: the world map's coastlines, at 1:110m, for Astro's grey
  line. Ships with the application. Public domain; made with Natural Earth.
<!-- credit: icons -->
- **Font Awesome Free, by Fonticons, Inc.**: the navigation icons. CC BY 4.0,
  as recorded above.
